#!/bin/sh
# SessionStart hook: RTL project orchestration rules injection
# Fires when the project carries a RAT marker (.rat/ or legacy .rtl-agent-team/).
# Injects critical design rules, delegation guidance, and pipeline context.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS:
# Plugin CLAUDE.md is NOT loaded in user projects — only skills, agents, hooks,
# and MCP servers are loaded from plugins. This hook replaces CLAUDE.md's function
# by auto-injecting the routing rules and pipeline rules that Claude needs to
# correctly orchestrate RTL design tasks.
#
# OUTPUT FORMAT (since v0.10.3):
# Claude Code's SessionStart hook validator requires JSON output with a
# `hookSpecificOutput.hookEventName` field. The routing markdown is delivered
# inside `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` (a JSON-escaped string).
# JSON encoding is performed at sync time by `scripts/sync_orchestrator_inject.sh`,
# so this script only needs to emit a pre-encoded JSON line — no runtime jq /
# python dependency. The single-quoted `cat << 'JSON_EOF'` heredoc preserves all
# bytes literally, including escape sequences inside the JSON string.

# Consume stdin (hook protocol)
INPUT=$(cat)
SCRIPT_DIR=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)
. "$SCRIPT_DIR/lib/rat-dir-util.sh"
. "$SCRIPT_DIR/lib/json-util.sh"
jsonu_detect_parser
CWD=$(jsonu_get_root_string "$INPUT" cwd)
[ -z "$CWD" ] && CWD="$(pwd)"

# RAT project marker: .rat/ (current) or .rtl-agent-team/ (legacy v0.8.11-).
# These directories are created by rtl-agent-team skills (including
# rat-init-project) when first invoked. Their presence means the project
# has actively used rtl-agent-team at least once. Generic directory names
# like rtl/ or docs/ are NOT used as markers — too many false positives.
# rat_is_project finds the marker by the rule every RAT hook uses
# (hooks/lib/rat-dir-util.sh), including the RAT_PROJECT_ROOT override.
#
# When no marker is present, emit minimal valid SessionStart JSON and exit
# silently. Per-skill init advisory (when a user invokes a rtl-agent-team
# skill in an unmarked project) is handled by rtl-skill-activation.sh.
if ! rat_is_project "$CWD"; then
  printf '{"hookSpecificOutput":{"hookEventName":"SessionStart"}}'
  exit 0
fi

# BEGIN GENERATED ROUTING BLOCK - sync via scripts/sync_orchestrator_inject.sh
cat << 'JSON_EOF'
{"hookSpecificOutput": {"hookEventName": "SessionStart", "additionalContext": "# RTL Agent Team — Active Project Rules\n\n## Pipeline Rules (Rule 5 hard-enforced; others advisory)\n1. No RTL coding without specification (run spec-analyst first) — policy\n2. No Testbench without Reference Model — policy\n3. No synthesis without RTL code — policy\n4. No Formal verification without passing Lint — policy (skill warning)\n5. **No completion after RTL modification without functional verification** (lint alone is insufficient) — HARD (rtl-verify-stop-gate.sh)\n6. No Phase 5 without per-module unit tests upon Phase 4 completion + Stream B early verification artifacts — policy (skill warning)\n7. Phase 5 FAIL → max 2 Phase 4 feedback loops; escalate to user if exceeded — policy (orchestrator counter)\n8. No Phase 6 without Phase 5 PASS (final-compliance.md verdict=PASS required) — policy (skill warning)\n9. Phase 7 is exempt — free exploration allowed without pipeline Gate\n10. No DC-based PPA optimization without Phase 5 PASS — policy (skill warning)\n11. Every PPA-Opt iteration must pass equivalence + smoke before the patch is accepted; on failure, roll back — policy (orchestrator guard)\n\n## Iron Requirements Protocol\n- Each phase produces iron-requirements.json (binding constraints for downstream) and open-requirements.json (homework for next phase)\n- Iron requirements from upper phases MUST NOT be violated\n- Authority hierarchy: P1(functional) > P2(architecture) > P3(micro-arch)\n- Violation triggers graduated escalation; infeasibility triggers Upstream Challenge with quantitative PPA evidence\n- Phase exit requires compliance-checker PASS against all upstream iron\n\n## Routing (key patterns → Action Skill)\nAlways route user intent to Action Skills first. Orchestrators are internal and spawned by skills.\n| Pattern | Route To |\n|---|---|\n| RTL design, chip design, full pipeline | `/rtl-agent-team:rat-auto-design` |\n| setup tools, EDA setup, install tools | `/rtl-agent-team:rat-setup` |\n| init project, initialize project, new project | `/rtl-agent-team:rat-init-project` |\n| debug, diagnostics, plugin status | `/rtl-agent-team:rat-plugin-debug` |\n| tutorial, getting started, how to use | `/rtl-agent-team:rat-tutorial` |\n| spec analysis, requirements, research | `/rtl-agent-team:p1-spec-research` |\n| codec, H.264, H.265, domain expert | `/rtl-agent-team:domain-consult` |\n| architecture design (RTL context) | `/rtl-agent-team:p2-arch-design` |\n| architecture review | `/rtl-agent-team:arch-review` |\n| reference model, C model | `/rtl-agent-team:ref-model` |\n| BFM, bus functional model, SystemC | `/rtl-agent-team:bfm-develop` |\n| microarchitecture, uarch | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-p3-uarch-design` |\n| DSE, design space exploration | `/rtl-agent-team:rat-dse` |\n| Phase 1 team, research team, parallel research | `/rtl-agent-team:p1-spec-research` team mode |\n| Phase 2 team, arch team, parallel architecture | `/rtl-agent-team:p2-arch-design` team mode |\n| Phase 3 team, uarch team, parallel uarch | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-p3-uarch-design` team mode |\n| refc to RTL, C model to hardware, refc to P5, refc를 RTL로 구현 | `/rtl-agent-team:rat-refc-to-p5` |\n| spec to uarch team, Phase 1-3 team | `/rtl-agent-team:rat-p1p3-spec-uarch` team mode |\n| spec to uarch, Phase 1-3, design only | `/rtl-agent-team:rat-p1p3-spec-uarch` |\n| uarch to verify, Phase 4-5, RTL from uarch | `/rtl-agent-team:rat-p4p5-impl-verify` |\n| RD eval, BD-PSNR, codec quality | `/rtl-agent-team:codec-rd-eval` |\n| decoder conformance, conformance stream | `/rtl-agent-team:codec-conformance-eval` |\n| rapid rtl, P4 rapid, sanity integration, fast implementation loop | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-p4-rapid-impl` |\n| bug fix, RTL fix, RTL bug | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-p4s-bugfix` |\n| RTL coding, module implementation | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-p4-implement` |\n| Phase 4 team, implement team, parallel implement | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-p4-implement` team mode |\n| block parallel, worktree parallel, 6-block | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-p4-block-parallel` |\n| refactoring (RTL context) | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-p4s-refactor` |\n| unit test (RTL context) | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-p4s-unit-test` |\n| IP instance, IP integration | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-ip-instantiate` |\n| lint, lint check | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-lint-check` |\n| synthesis, yosys, SDC | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-synth-check` |\n| RTL documentation | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-document` |\n| IP-XACT, register map | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-ipxact-gen` |\n| functional closure, P5A, deep functional verification, hierarchical functional closure | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-p5a-functional-closure` |\n| silicon validation, P5B, signoff readiness, timing signoff, post-functional signoff | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-p5b-silicon-validation` |\n| Phase 5, verification pipeline | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-p5-verify` |\n| Phase 5 team, verify team, parallel verify | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-p5-verify` team mode |\n| simulation, testbench, cocotb | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-p5s-func-verify` |\n| UVM verification, sequence, agent | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-p5s-uvm-verify` |\n| performance verification, throughput | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-p5s-perf-verify` |\n| formal, SVA, assertion | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-p5s-sva-check` |\n| CDC, clock domain | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-p5s-cdc-verify` |\n| AXI, APB, AHB, protocol | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-p5s-protocol-verify` |\n| coverage | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-p5s-coverage-analyze` |\n| PPA optimize, DC PPA, power/timing/area optimize | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-ppa-optimize-dc` |\n| PPA auto-loop, ultraloop PPA, converge PPA | `/rtl-agent-team:rat-ultraloop-ppa` |\n| integration test, cross-module, Tier 4 | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-p5s-integration-test` |\n| regression, multi-seed | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-p5s-func-verify` (Tier 3) |\n| RTL conformance, golden comparison | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-conformance-test` |\n| bug reproduction, waveform debug | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-bug-repro` |\n| model consistency, RTL-model compare | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-model-consistency` |\n| cross-phase contract, spec consistency | `/rtl-agent-team:cross-phase-contract-validator` |\n| design review, Phase 6, design note | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-p6-design-review` |\n| exploration, Phase 7, free exploration | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-p7-exploration` |\n| ultraloop, autonomous loop, unattended | `/rtl-agent-team:rat-ultraloop` |\n| LLM code review, safe refactor, review and refactor workflow | `/rtl-agent-team:rtl-review-refactor` |\n| cross-review, codex review, 2nd reviewer, second opinion | `/rtl-agent-team:codex-cross-review` |\n| `.sv/.svh/.v/.vh` files | `systemverilog` (agent-loaded) |\n| `.sv/.sva` assertion work | `systemverilog-assertion` (agent-loaded) |\n| UVM testbench generation | `uvm` (agent-loaded) |\n| `.cpp/.h` SystemC/TLM work | `systemc` (agent-loaded) |\nConvention skills are loaded by writer agents via their `skills:` frontmatter (rtl-coder→systemverilog, bfm-dev→systemc, testbench-dev/sva-extractor/protocol-checker→systemverilog-assertion/uvm); naming basics also enforced by the deployed `.claude/rules` file on .sv access.\nInternal routing reference skill (`rtl-orchestrate`) is non-user-invocable and loaded by agents when needed.\n\n## Agent dispatch\nResolve worker tiers using `{plugin_root}/runtime/model-selection.md` for the active host. Inherit the session model when no suitable ID is available.\nPhase owners use `{plugin_root}/runtime/phase-dispatch.md` for project-enabled or explicitly requested Codex reviews.\n\n## Core Design Principles\n- **Hierarchical Spec Compliance**: Lower stages must never violate upper stage specs. Spec → Arch → μArch → RTL → Verify. Changes require returning upstream.\n- **Light review**: One review against the evidence, then stop and name the open items. A further round only when the user asks. With no measurement, the model's confidence is the gate: one spec reading, or one architecture choice, passes. Do not iterate to raise it. Low confidence is asked once. Lint, simulation, formal, coverage, synthesis, CDC, and model comparison are judged from the measured result. Confidence does not override a measurement. Prompts state the goal, the constraints, the evidence, and the done condition. Do not add step-by-step scaffolding for judgment work. Leave effort at the session default.\n- **Judgment and ambiguity**: Record confidence and the evidence for a decision. Check whether different readings change behavior, interfaces, constraints, or a verification expected result. An unresolved material ambiguity stays open, regardless of an average score. Ask once when a user decision is needed and continue independent work. Keep project contracts and task-specific source facts; do not teach general RTL knowledge or force a fixed exploration method.\n- **Document-as-Memory**: Design artifacts serve as persistent memory across phases. Each phase reads upstream docs, writes downstream. Enables resumability.\n- **Asymmetric Phase Gate**: Exit gates enforce artifact existence (strict). Entry gates scan and warn but proceed with available artifacts (flexible). Feedback loops capped at 2 iterations before user escalation.\n- **Cross-Phase Artifact Functional Consistency**: Verification artifacts (P2 refC, P3 BFM, P4 unit tests, P5 TBs) must be functionally validated against upstream references via output comparison — not just file existence + compilation. BFM that compiles but produces wrong output → FAIL.\n\n## Coding Conventions (Core Overrides — .sv/.svh/.v/.vh)\nPort prefix `i_`/`o_`/`io_` (NOT suffix; clk/rst exempt). Clock `clk`/`{domain}_clk`, reset `rst_n`/`{domain}_rst_n` (active-low async). snake_case only (no CamelCase); params ALL_CAPS, localparam `L_` prefix. Full rules auto-load from `.claude/rules/rtl-coding-conventions.md` on .sv access (deployed by rat-init-project).\n\n## Mandatory Verification After RTL Changes\nRTL modify → configured lint → TB create/update → simulation PASS → done\nGate: `scripts/run_sim.sh` records `.rat/state/verify-evidence.json`; completion requires a measured PASS bound to the current inputs and logs. A waiver for non-functional changes (`.rat/state/rtl-verify-waiver`) is the user's decision; ask first. Both are in the project root's `.rat/state/`, not in a subdirectory the session cd'd into.\n\n## 6+1 Phase Design Pipeline\nP1: Research → P2: Arch/Ref → P3: μArch → P4: RTL+Unit → P5: Verify → P6: Design Note → P7: Exploration (optional)\nArtifacts: `docs/phase-N-*/` (design guides), `reviews/phase-N-*/` (verdicts)\n"}}
JSON_EOF
# END GENERATED ROUTING BLOCK
